# guard-generated.globs — paths a fail-closed preToolUse hook forbids hand-editing (constitution P4).
#
# CONSUMER-OWNED. Every line here is yours; a framework upgrade must never overwrite this file, which
# is also why the hook's own self-protection is NOT here — `.claude/hooks/*` is denied by a built-in
# rule in `scripts/guard-generated.sh` instead, so it reaches every consumer including the ones that
# never create this file. See the "Rule 1" block there.
#
# One glob per line. `*` spans `/` (bash [[ ]] semantics, so `libs/api/src/*` matches any depth).
# Lines starting with `#` are comments; blank lines are ignored. `guard-generated.sh` DENIES a
# Write/Edit whose target path matches any active glob.
#
# The framework ships this EMPTY (every example commented) — the P4 guard is inert until a consumer
# repo uncomments/sets its own generated paths. Enable per repo:
#
# Typical Java/Gradle setup (adjust to your repo). Written build-anchored rather than as a bare
# `*/generated/*`, so a real source package that happens to be named `generated` is not caught.
#
#   OpenAPI server stubs + DTOs generated into <module>/build/generated. Regenerate by editing the
#   spec in the contract repo and re-running the build, never by editing the output.
*/build/generated/*
build/generated/*
#
#   XJC / JAXB types compiled from XSD + WSDL into <module>/build/generated-sources. Same
#   contract-first argument: the XSD/WSDL is the source.
*/build/generated-sources/*
build/generated-sources/*

# Other examples, left commented:
#   Frontend — a generated OpenAPI client (e.g. ng-openapi-gen):
# libs/api/src/*
#
#   Contract repo — generated artefacts, if any:
# gen/*
